WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.100
Kanuka's Report

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.020
I'm grateful for all your help.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.400
Think your training here
was worthwhile?

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.360
Yes, definitely.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.990
We'll have to have
a farewell party for you.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.580
Please don't;
I'll say goodbye to everyone.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.910
I'm no good at dealing with
mushy Japanese sentimentality.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:30.420
Besides, I still need
to finish my report.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.540
- Oh.
- I'll be off, then.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.550
I wasn't here long,
but I truly am indebted.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.060
No good at sentimentality?

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.310
Foreigners are so reserved.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:51.520
Maybe she just doesn't
want to appear weak.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.310
Even now that she's leaving.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.860
Reminds me of
someone else I know.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.760
We will conduct
a Labor combat tournament.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:24.550
The results will determine your
positions within our Pat Division...

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:26.970
so do your best.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.060
Any questions?

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:29.890
Yes! Over here!

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:32.390
All in good time.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.520
Captain!

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.980
I know, you don't have to say it.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.950
I'm Lieutenant Kanuka Clancy,
of the New York City Police.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.330
I've come to Japan
for advanced training.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.910
Pleased to meet you.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.450
New York?

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.750
- All rise!
- Why, what's going on?

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.500
Pay your respects to
the police lieutenant!

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.880
Ota, don't get your shorts in a knot.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.170
But, Captain!

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.060
People, the time has come!

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:18.320
Prepare to commence Plan 908!

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.190
Right!

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.280
Officer Izumi, hitting the trail!

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.450
They're up to something again.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.740
I figured they might be, but...

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:29.410
What?

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.790
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.220
Now, I will announce
your positions in the Pat Division.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.220
Number one Forward Ingram Pilot:
Officer Noa Izumi.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:53.100
Number one Backup, command
car: Officer Asuma Shinohara.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.940
Number one Labor carrier:
Officer: Hiromi Yamazaki.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:00.770
Number two Forward, Ingram
pilot: Officer Isao Ota.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.990
Backup, command car:
Lieutenant Kanuka Clancy.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:08.490
Labor carrier:
Officer Mikiyasu Shinshi.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.490
That is all.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.080
Ota, any idea why
I chose you as the forward?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.210
Yes, Sir!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:20.710
Because I can't give orders
to Lieutenant Clancy!

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:21.920
Wrong!

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.760
It's because I'll only
be here for six months.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:29.220
And you shouldn't adapt
the Ingram to temporary staff.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.260
Six months, huh...

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.350
It'll be an interesting six months.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.030
Noa here. The subject has
entered a department store.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.450
- Over.
- Roger.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.830
Stay on her trail, Izumi.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:56.790
No luck?

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.710
Isn't this against the law?

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:01.750
Only criminals can commit crimes!

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.090
There's an interesting theory.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.340
What's your problem?
We're the police!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.350
Sorry to disturb you.
We'll be done soon.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.770
You're so slow that you've
disturbed this taxpayer!

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.150
Stand back and learn!

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.360
No, you've gotta be more gentle!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:28.360
Locks are so fragile these days.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:31.070
Sorry! We'll fix it later!

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.920
Don't draw it out
any longer than you have to!

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.300
Use your gun
and shoot his legs out.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.850
I can handle this my way!

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.490
I ordered you to fire!

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.160
The Labor didn't do anything wrong!

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.450
His <i>pilot</i> was the problem!

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.410
You're too lenient!

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:25.630
You aren't authorized to ignore
orders from the command car!

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:29.340
That's enough.
Give it a rest, ladies.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:31.470
But, Captain!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.050
Enough.
Both of you write up reports.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.560
Have them on my desk today.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.430
Ota, calm down!

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:42.560
Ota!

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:46.020
Yamazaki, get out of my way
if you don't wanna get shot!

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.190
You don't have the guts to fire!

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:49.900
We'll see about that!

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:50.900
Stop it!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.460
Homework.
Have them on my desk first thing.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:07.960
Yes, Sir!

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.350
How's everything looking?

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:19.520
Pretty good, I'd say!

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.430
Yeah, not bad!

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.770
"Kanuka Clancy's Farewell Party."

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.860
Good work!

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.070
Mission accomplished!

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.400
Let's crack a beer!

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.400
Shouldn't we wait for Kanuka?

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:36.160
No problem, as long
as we don't touch the cake.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.030
I'm for that.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:39.950
Hey, look at this.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:41.450
What's up?

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.080
What is it?

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:46.500
"Training Report:
Special Vehicles, Section 2."

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:50.420
This is the report Kanuka's
submitting in New York.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.300
It's in English.
What's it say?

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:03.890
"PatLabor Division 2 consists
of several unique characters."

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:06.940
It's the captain!

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:11.020
"When he was with the
Metropolitan Police Department...

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.280
he was called 'Razor Sharp Goto.'

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.860
He was on the fast track
until he left to run Division 2."

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.280
Come and face me, Goto!

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.740
It's Judgment Day, my friend!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.870
Come quietly, Goto!

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.580
Don't go, Captain.
It's too dangerous!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:36.090
Captain!

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:37.300
Goto!

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:40.970
Chew on this!

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:54.360
Everyone's against me!
Don't move an inch!

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:57.610
I'll get you this time!
I'll get you!

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:08.210
It took a lot of guts to
face him down like that.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:10.670
Oh, that.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:15.420
Well, Sakaki had told me their
Labor was completely harmless.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:18.380
He could tell that?

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:19.380
Guess so.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.050
You're impossible.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:26.600
What will your adoring fans say?

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.600
Who knows?

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.060
That cheater!

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:34.230
"As the Japanese say, he's, 'Useless
as a lamp in broad daylight.'

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:36.530
And whether or not he's as sharp
as a razor, is yet to be determined."

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.530
Hey, does she mention me?

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:42.320
"A true Japanese policeman."

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.490
Or maybe, "the world's only
one-man army of justice!"

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:45.950
Hold your horses.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.750
Hey, don't look!

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.420
No probs; we're just having fun.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:52.580
"Officer Mikiyasu Shinshi.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.750
He left a trading firm
to serve as a police officer.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.920
The only married
man in Division 2."

00:10:59.550 --> 00:10:59.880
Bow!

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.770
Ready to give in yet?

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:10.730
You cheated! You coward!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.900
Whatever it takes to win!

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:20.650
So you think this is funny?

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:28.080
What do you think is so funny?

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.960
Stop! Bow first
and start all over!

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:40.470
What's so funny?

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.340
Stop it!

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.300
Funny now? Funny now?

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:49.270
Are you trying to kill me?

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:51.480
Officer Shinshi, you're disqualified!

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:57.110
"He's what they call in Japan
a 'backfire."'

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:01.610
Who's next?

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.360
Let's stop this.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:04.950
Quitting now?

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.330
You make a fool of me,
then want to quit?

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.460
Asuma's up next!

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.670
"Asuma Shinohara's father
founded Shinohara Industries...

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:21.760
developer and
manufacturer of Labors.

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:26.470
Asuma joined Division 2 after
a falling out with his father."

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:27.850
What do you think?

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:30.560
This one is extremely popular.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.600
You're kidding!

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.230
Well, don't read my section!

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:38.020
Easier said! Shinshi's drunk
and I can't stop him!

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:38.940
Crap!

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:54.710
Ingram Unit 3

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:09.970
Kanuka Clancy... Kanuka Clancy...

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:11.970
Apartment 302!

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.730
C'mon! C'mon!

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.690
Uh, hello.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:32.160
You're just in time;
we're about to read your file!

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.330
Oh, really?

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:40.630
"Officer Noa Izumi,
pilot of Ingram unit 1."

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:43.590
Noa Izumi reporting for duty
with the Patrol Labors!

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:48.590
Give me back my PatLabor!

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:02.940
I won't let you get away!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:13.200
I did it!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.130
Ah, the smell of a new car!

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:46.230
Alphonse.

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:56.290
This is a dream come true!

00:14:56.290 --> 00:15:01.250
Mine

00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:02.330
"She's emotionally attached to a mare
tool with the various mechanisms.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.750
She lavishes affection on her Labor
as if it were a favorite pet.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:09.800
There's a fine line between
her hobby and her work...

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.090
and between whether
she's happy or miserable."

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:17.930
Is that supposed to
be praise or an insult?

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:19.980
Neither.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:23.270
She wrote that because
you're such a slip-shod officer!

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.360
Oh, look! Hiromi's next!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:37.990
"Insufficient data."

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.870
That's why I told you
to skip ahead to me!

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:43.710
Okay, here you are!

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:47.500
"Officer Isao Ota,
pilot of unit 2.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:53.340
Excessively violent, but
a better marksman than Izumi.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:54.840
On the other hand..."

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:58.010
I'll blow you away!

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:05.650
My gun! Where's my gun?

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:10.240
- Ota, watch your left!
- The left!

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:20.910
Ammo!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:23.210
You don't have any extra ammo!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:26.080
What's with the lousy aim?

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.710
We don't have any more ammunition,
thanks to you!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.340
Then I'll use brute force!

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.020
"It is a miracle that...

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:48.940
this man was ever allowed
to join the police.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:53.900
He's an armed lunatic,
a walking powder keg...

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.610
and a stubborn fool.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:58.620
But whatever else
he may be called...

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:01.410
he might best be described as...

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.410
a psycho cop."

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:12.460
That's preposterous!

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.180
You broke it!

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:23.850
Kanuka's going to be mad
when she gets back!

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.310
- What'll we do?
- Run away!

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:29.190
Why us?
You're the one that broke it, Ota.

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:31.570
She's not gonna care about
the little details!

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:35.070
Clean this mess
if you value your lives!

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.030
We have to wipe off the prints!

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:39.740
- Gimme a break.
- This is definitely a crime.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:59.010
This is terrible!

00:17:59.010 --> 00:17:59.680
What's wrong?

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:04.270
Some suspicious men like this
broke into your apart...

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:05.890
Don't worry, I'll handle it.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:14.070
The lock's been forced.
It must be terrorists!

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:28.040
Hold it!

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:46.060
H-H-Hello? Is this the police?

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:49.140
Breaking and entering!
Property destruction!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:50.520
Invasion of privacy!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.020
You call yourselves cops?

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:53.060
Well, actually...

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:54.980
Save your excuses!
Get out!

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:58.490
Thanks for your hospitality!

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:05.200
Terrorist bombers at
Officer Clancy's apartment?

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.040
No, I won't need any backup.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:12.000
I'm sure we can handle it.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.960
Yes, right. I understand.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:17.340
So your concern was justified?

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:18.760
Yup.

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:23.890
Reports

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.840
I'm gonna need more of these.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:27.060
So you're an armed lunatic
and a walking powder keg...

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:28.850
but isn't it about time
to mellow out?

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:30.230
Shut up!

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:32.810
You wanted to read it too!
And you too!

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:35.320
What, you're blaming it on me?

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:37.280
It's not my fault!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:41.740
Let's just drop it.
Man, what a horrible farewell party.

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:44.660
Well, you were supposed
to be TRAILING her!

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:46.490
That's right!
It's YOUR fault!

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:50.250
Now who's calling
the kettle black, Ota?

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.880
You're the one who went nuts
on the computer!

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.380
In conclusion:

00:19:55.750 --> 00:20:01.420
Division 2 is composed of
truly unique officers.

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:05.850
Creative, audacious, impulsive...

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:10.060
daring, impudent, disrespectful...

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:13.650
reckless, destructive, arrogant...

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:17.110
thoughtless, short-tempered!

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:22.570
That covers the major
flaws in their organization.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:37.130
Good luck, Kanuka

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:53.100
However, their performance far
exceeds my original expectations.

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:26.150
In short, their qualities
can be summed up as...

00:22:42.540 --> 00:22:45.760
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.880 --> 00:22:49.470
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.800 --> 00:22:55.720
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:05.230
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:08.150
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.240 --> 00:23:12.740
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:17.410
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:20.250
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:24.420
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:30.930
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:36.180
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:38.720
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:41.940
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:46.020
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.400 --> 00:23:52.200
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.370 --> 00:23:58.240
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
